# Repo-root .dockerignore (AS-37).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT THE REPO ROOT. apps/invoicing builds with
# `context: ../..` (the repo root) so the Dockerfile can COPY the single
# source of visual truth, docs/design/tokens/tokens.css, without checking a
# second copy of it into the app (plan §5.3). Docker resolves .dockerignore
# against the build context, so a repo-root context means THIS file — and
# there was none before this task.
#
# This is a correctness file, not a speed file: the raw context is only ~10 MB.
# The line that matters is apps/chat/data — without it, the company's LIVE
# internal chat database is baked into the product image.
#
# apps/chat is unaffected: apps/chat/compose.yaml builds with `context: .`
# (= apps/chat), so it keeps using apps/chat/.dockerignore. Nothing else in
# the repo builds from the repo root.
#
# Pinned by apps/invoicing/test/deploy-shape.test.js — update both together.
#
# **/.env.local (AS-38): the optional, gitignored file a developer keeps a Stripe
# test key in. It is read by `docker compose --env-file`, never by a Dockerfile;
# a build context is the one place it could be copied into an image by accident.
.git
.worktrees
**/node_modules
apps/chat/data
.claude
**/.env.local
